  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ram1424/Memory-Trail/zipball/v1.4",
  "body": "Memory Trails 1.4 for macOS.\nBuild: 8\n\nHighlights:\n- Memory Trails 1.4 promotes the polished 1.3 feature set into a new major point release with a cleaner, release-style What’s New experience.\n- Outlook capture includes the latest Classic and New Outlook reliability improvements, support for column and non-column layouts, calendar invitations, sender-aware timeline entries, and stronger protection against Outlook UI chrome being logged as email data.\n- Today & Timeline include the restored details experience, Go to Today, clearer activity presentation, and improved app-name handling.\n- Ask Memory Trails returns uncapped matching Supporting Activity, includes Back to Top navigation, clearer quick-start icons, and expanded activity Close controls.\n- Insights, Favorites, Clipboard History, Storage/History/Export, Settings, update handling, and privacy-first local processing refinements are included.\n- Version 1.4 remains local-first: no cloud timeline sync, external data connectors, advertising SDKs, or AI timeline summarization.\n\n\nPrivacy:\n- Captured activity is sourced, processed, and stored locally on the Mac.\n- No cloud timeline sync.\n- No external data connectors.\n- No analytics or advertising SDKs.\n- No Memory Trails account or remote account is required.\n- Captured timeline data is not transmitted to an external service.\n- Passwords and Wallet are excluded by default.\n- Clipboard capture can be disabled at any time.\n- Apps and processes can be excluded from capture.\n- Source code is available in this repository for review and verification.\n- Memory Trails does not generate AI summaries of the timeline.\n\nRequires macOS 14 or later. Detailed window/activity capture requires Accessibility permission.\n\nThis automated build uses ad-hoc signing when a Developer ID certificate is not configured and is not notarized in that case."
